# Per-package USE for flags that are not worth setting globally.
#
# Measured, not guessed: each flag below appears in the IUSE of at most six
# packages in ::gentoo + ::pwr. A global USE entry for a flag that six packages
# have read is noise — it makes the profile's USE list look like policy when
# it is really a handful of per-package settings, and it hides the flags that
# genuinely are policy.
#
# Counts are from a scan of every md5-cache entry in both repos, 2026-08-04.
# Regenerate the census if the tree moves on; a flag that grows consumers
# belongs back in PROF_LIVE_USE.

app-admin/testdisk ntfs reiserfs
app-arch/wimlib ntfs
app-cdr/graveman dvdr
app-editors/vim vim-pager
app-eselect/eselect-repository mercurial
app-laptop/laptop-mode-tools acpi
